<title>USA: Southern National sets buyback for merger.</title>
<headline>Southern National sets buyback for merger.</headline>
<dateline>WINSTON-SALEM, N.C. 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern National Corp said Friday it would repurchase between 1.7 million and 2.1 million of its shares for reissue in connection with its proposed acquisition of Fidelity Financial Bankshares Corp .</p>
<p>Southern National said it anticipates issuing between 1.7 million and 2.1 million shares in the merger. The exact number will depend on adjustment to the exchange ratio, it said.  </p>
<p>As a result of the repurchase, the acquisition of Fidelity Financial will be accounted for as a purchase, instead of as a pooling of interests as originally announced.</p>
<p>Southern National said the stock repurchase will allow it to manage its capital position better and improve per-share earnings.</p>
</text>
